      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The overtones, or partials, are essentially the higher-frequency vibrations present in a sound wave beyond the basic fundamental frequency. These harmonics give a flute its unique \"timbre,\" allowing you to distinguish it from another instrument producing the same fundamental pitch. Richer and more complex overtones lead to a brighter, more resonant, or \"flutey\" sound character.",
