    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but are there certain overtones that don't always sound \"clean\"? like, are there any frequencies that feel out of place or give the instrument a more \"ghostly\" or unpredictable quality?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, those irregular overtones are known as inharmonic partials, and they are what introduce spectral complexity beyond simple tuning. If these inharmonic frequencies are particularly strong or mistuned relative to the fundamental, they can contribute to beating, dissonance, or a wavering, \"ghostly\" quality. Pure tones have predictable, integer multiples of the fundamental, while inharmonicity disrupts that pleasing harmonic series.",
